comments.body:
@grubernaut I've attempted to do things the way you mentioned multiple times but I keep coming back to this.

Basically I think that @moudixtc is right and `aws_iam_policy_attachment` is designed backwards from how most people would use it.

This means that there's simply no way for module authors to allow users of their module to pass in policy ARNs and hide the complexity of wiring up the resources the module creates and the policies the users have passed in.
